cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "emerging-market-skills: agent skills for building software under emerging-market constraints"
message: "If you use these skills in research or in a published product, please cite them."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kaguara
    given-names: Antony Muroki
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kaguara/emerging-market-skills"
abstract: >-
  A set of AI agent skills encoding engineering constraints for products built
  for emerging-market users: intermittent and expensive connectivity, entry-level
  devices, per-action integration costs, and interfaces used by people with
  varying literacy and prior exposure to software. Each skill pairs prose
  guidance with machine-readable rules and runnable validators.
keywords:
  - emerging markets
  - offline-first
  - mobile development
  - agent skills
  - performance budgets
  - internationalization
license: MIT
